      "calculationScope": "EXACT_MANUAL_CALCULATION",
      "manualArithmetic": "No assigned numerical exercise. A linear steady slab profile gives Fourier power-lambda*A*dT/dx=lambda*A(Th-Tc)/s. Double thickness halves power; double area and thickness cancel. Reviewer toy:lambda1/2W/(mK),area2m²,deltaT20K,s1/10m gives200W. Density contrast1000minus990kg/m³ over1L in assignedg10 gives upwardbuoyancy1/10N as a possible natural-convection driver. Radiation uses absolute fourth powers: equalbody/environmentT givesnetzero, doubledbodyT versusunchangedambient gives15ambient emissionunits net, whileemissionalone scales16. Shifting the arbitrary temperature origin changes the expression; Celsius cannot replacekelvin.",
      "manualFeasibility": "PASS_AI_EXACT",
      "physicalAssumptions": "One-dimensional homogeneous slab,positiveconstant/effectiveconductivity,steadyfixedfacetemperatures,negligiblelateral losses,positiveelapsedtime. Th>Tc fixespositiveconductedpower. Naturalconvectionneedsgravityanddensitycontrast;not everyhotparcelnecessarilyrises. Greybodyconstantemissivity[0,1] inlargeisothermalenclosure,absolute temperatures,netoutward sign. Absorption/emissionmaybothnonzerowhilenetzero. Electromagnetictransportdoesnotneedmaterialmedium.",
